<Docs title="Troubleshooting" description="Common problems and how to resolve them when using RUDRA." slug="troubleshooting">
  <p class="lead">Solutions to common issues when installing and using the toolchain.</p>

  <h2>rudra: command not found</h2>
  <p>The install directory is not on your PATH. The Linux installer places binaries in <code>~/.local/bin</code> by default. Add it to your PATH and open a new terminal.</p>
  <CodeBlock lang="sh" code={`export PATH="$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH"
rudra version`} />

  <h2>Type error: argument of 'len' expects str</h2>
  <p><code>len</code> operates on strings. It does not take an array. This is a compile-time type error and is expected.</p>

  <h2>type error: there is no function named 'send'</h2>
  <p>Channel send and receive are named <code>chan_send</code> and <code>chan_recv</code>. Functions named <code>send</code> and <code>recv</code> do not exist.</p>

  <h2>type error: there is no function named 'json_parse'</h2>
  <p>Use <code>json_get</code> to read a value from a JSON object. There is no <code>json_parse</code> function.</p>

  <h2>http_get returns an empty result for a hostname</h2>
  <p><code>http_get</code> does not resolve hostnames. Use a numeric IP address. HTTPS and TLS are not implemented.</p>

  <h2>Checksum does not match</h2>
  <p>Re-download the asset and verify again. Do not install an archive whose SHA256 does not match the value on the <a href="/downloads">Downloads</a> page.</p>
</Docs>
